WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.369
-Our first guest tonight is an
Emmy and Academy Award-winning

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.537
actor you know from
"Basic Instinct," "Wall Street,"

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.705 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and "Fatal Attraction."

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
He stars in the Netflix series
"The Kominsky Method,"

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.542 size:84% position:42% line:92%
which is streaming now.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.445
-You know, I wake up every
morning, and my first thought

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:15.081 size:81% position:41%
is, "What part of me
is not working today?"

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can I tell you a secret?
-Sure.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:21.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sometimes when I laugh
real hard, I fart a little.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.391
-Oh, please. You're still young.
Wait till you're my age.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:27.360
Every time I sneeze, I hear
rattling around in my hips.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
It feels like a foreign object
broken loose.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:34.601 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, we are passengers
on boats slowly sinking.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:38.104
-Please welcome back to the show
Michael Douglas, everyone.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.273 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:47.414 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:55.121 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
Welcome back.
-Thank you, Seth.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
Always a delight to have you.
-Thank you.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nice of you to have me.
It's been great.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a show
about people getting older.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:06.466
-About people getting older.
I don't know how they cast me.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:09.602
-Yeah. I can't figure this out.
They just came to me.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.839
I said, "This is a stretch, man.
This is a real stretch."

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, there is one thing
that would lead me to believe

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it would seem like
a stretch to you,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is your father,
Kirk Douglas --

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:19.679 line:92%
You're going back out to L.A.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is about to have
his 102nd birthday.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.784 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm going out --
I'm going out Sunday.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:30.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sunday, he's 102.
-102, which is, I mean --

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.759
What a gift to you and your
family to still have him around.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Except I'm afraid it's
a generation skipping thing.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-My kids are in good shape.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
Me, I'm not so sure.
-Right.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:40.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're already casting you
as an old guy.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.536 size:84% position:42%
Your dad's still alive.
It's not fair at all.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you do
for a 102nd birthday?

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, not much.
Not much, you know?

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:52.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
No. First thing is very smart.
We're making it for lunch.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, there you go.
-You know, make it good.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:57.484
And then that lets him go out
and not do his favorite line,

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.886 size:81% position:41%
which he's been doing
for the last 30 years,

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is...
"I'm late for the disco."

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we'll have a good time.
You know, he's amazing.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's is --
Actually I blame myself.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:11.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has discovered FaceTime.
-Oh, wow. Gotcha.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's all great
except, you know,

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
I live on the East coast,
so he hasn't --

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's kind of forgot
about the time change,

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
the three-hour time change.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:21.207 line:92%
So, he likes dinner 7:30, 8:00.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.442 line:92%
And Catherine and I, we're up --

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:26.446
We're to bed early, you know, so
it's like 10:30, 11:00 at night.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:27.914 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So, I'll get a ring.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hi, Dad."
"Where are you?"

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "I'm in bed, Dad.
I'm in bed."

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:36.256 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Let me see." You know?

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.223 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I know where he's going.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:40.960
I said, "I know -- You just want
to see Catherine, don't you?"

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So poor Catherine,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's got to fluff her hair up
and everything.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.798 line:92%
"Hi, Kirk!" You know, like...

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She has to get
hair and makeup for bed.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.435 size:84% position:42% line:92%
That's not fair at all.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.737 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-No, it's rough. Rough.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:53.406
-So, do you think that --
Going back to the show,

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.942
obviously, it's a comedy,
it's about getting older.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you find getting older
has humor to it?

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has that been your experience
thus far?

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:03.316
-Well, that's why I'm doing the
show, to find that humor.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.684 line:92%
It's produced by Chuck Lorre.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A very funny man.
-Yeah, pretty good.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, great -- you know,
going back to "Dharma &amp; Greg,"

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.256 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"Two and a Half Men,"

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Big Bang Theory,"
"Young Sheldon."

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.961
But it's in the streaming
situation, which is really cool,

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
because there's
no commercials, right?

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:18.665 line:92%
It can be a half-hour comedy.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
It can be 20 minutes one week,
40 minutes the next.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:24.604
But the purpose when I read
it -- it's a great script --

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
was finding the humor
in getting old.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"I think I got to read this.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.577 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I got to work on that."

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so we got an unbelievable
response already,

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably more than any picture
I've ever had.

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:35.848 size:84% position:42%
-Oh, that's fantastic.
-I'm enjoying it a lot.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:39.719
Alan Arkin's a lovely partner
to work with. And here we go.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:42.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Another one of your co-stars
is Danny DeVito,

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
who you have
a long history with,

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you put him
in "Cuckoo's Nest."

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.695 size:81% position:41%
You worked together in
"Romancing the Stone."

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:49.395 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Is it true --

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because that is a movie
that means a great deal to me.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it true that he,
Danny DeVito --

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've heard him say this,
and I don't know,

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
how good a source he is --

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.440 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that he saved your life.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.274 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Did he save your life?

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:05.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't believe that
he gets away with this story.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:07.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-He -- Yes.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had -- we were down
in "Romancing the Stone,"

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a snake bit me,
and it bit me on the arm.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.321
Right?
Now, that was the extent of it.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.724
Danny, on the other hand,
says that he reached over

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:22.128
and he sucked the blood out
of the snake wound on my arm.

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:26.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then he says, "Can you imagine
if it was on his balls?!"

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.002 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:29.969 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I said, "Danny..."

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, what he'll do
for a joke. I don't know.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
-So none of this is true?

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.343
-No, no, I mean, he was there
when the snake bit me, you know?

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:41.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Didn't do anything, though?
-He didn't do nothing!

